condition_name: Kwashiorkor and Marasmus
condition_slug: kwashiorkor-and-marasmus
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "Adequate nutrition is the intake and utilization of energy-giving and body building foods and nutrients in the right proportions to maintain well-being, and productivity. Malnutrition manifests as stunting, underweight, wasting (kwashiorkor and marasmus), obesity as well as deficiencies of micronutrients."
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Kwashiorkor
    features[11]: Growth retardation,muscle wasting,anaemia,apathy,moon face,lack-luster skin,easily plucked hair,pedal oedema,hypo-pigmented skin patches,exfoliation,diarrhoea
  - type: Marasmus
    features[3]: Thin; protruding bones,"hungry-looking 'old-looking face,'",whimpering cry
investigations[7]: Full Blood Count,ESR,Stool microscopy,Urinalysis,Serum proteins,Chest radiograph,Mantoux test
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[3]: Nutritional counselling,"Adequate nutrient intake: may require assistance and special preparations e.g. nasogastric feeding",Periodic growth monitoring
  drug[1]: May be indicated where there are specific infections/infestations
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[0]:
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null